 8. Checks that the session-start hooks actually fired — gstack-execution's verification discipline and ponytail's restraint layer inject their rulesets at session start, and a hook that silently fails to fire looks exactly like one that fired with nothing to say. Reports active / NOT LOADED in the briefing's Shared services line, with the remedy when absent. Never gates the session.
+8b. Checks the model economy (ME-001, Dorian 2026-11-02): the standing rule is a cheaper main model with a stronger advisor, never the strongest model running throughout. Read `model` and `advisorModel` from `~/.claude/settings.json` and from the project's `.claude/settings.json` if present (project wins). Expected: `model` is `sonnet` (or a Sonnet model ID) and `advisorModel` is `fable` or `opus`. Report one line in Shared services: `Model economy: sonnet main + fable advisor` when both hold; `Model economy: NOT SET (main=<x>, advisor=<y>)` otherwise, followed by the remedy on its own line: `run /model sonnet, then /advisor fable (first time: /model fable once to accept the usage-credits consent, then back to /model sonnet)`. A session cannot switch its own model, so this reports; it never gates and never edits the settings file. If `DISABLE_TELEMETRY` or `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ADVISOR_TOOL` is set in the environment, say so: the advisor is off regardless of the setting. Whatever the setting says, apply the gstack-build economy inside this session: reading and mapping go to the `explore` and `docs` agents on Haiku; consult the advisor before committing to an approach and before declaring an item done; do not spend the main model on `grep | head`.
 9. Displays a structured briefing in chat with mounted folders, active subfolders, last-session handoff (open work + suggested opening line), top kanban tasks, recent decisions, and open PRs/issues.
